<clickhouse>

    <!--
      COLD S3 TIER AND S3 BACKUP DISK: DISABLED 2026-07-31.

      The Ace Cloud S3 bucket that backed both disks is being decommissioned, so
      every reference to its endpoint has been removed from this file. The
      template at the bottom is kept as a generic reference only; it carries a
      placeholder endpoint and will NOT work until a real one is filled in.

      Verified on prod (10.0.20.73) before disabling:
        * zero active parts on any non default disk, server wide
        * zero tables on the hot_cold or s3_policy storage policies
        * the only storage_policy in use by any MergeTree table is 'default'
        * no table's CREATE statement references the endpoint, cold_s3, or
          TO VOLUME

      The clickstream_data cold data was detached (not dropped) by
      scripts/detach_cold_parts.sh, so no S3 delete or fetch requests were
      issued. Those detached parts remain under the table's detached/ directory
      and cost about 17 MiB of local metadata in total. They can be removed with
      DROP DETACHED once the bucket is gone, or simply left in place.

      NOTE: the matching <backups><allowed_disk>s3_backup</allowed_disk> block in
      config/config.xml has also been commented out. It must stay commented while
      s3_backup is undefined, otherwise BACKUP/RESTORE points at a disk that does
      not exist.

      NOTE: the ACE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and ACE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY environment
      variables these disks used are no longer read by any config. They are not
      present in this repo's .env (which only carries AWS_*), so check the prod
      host's own environment and drop them there once the bucket is deleted.

      TO RE ENABLE object storage later, uncomment the block below and replace
      the placeholder values:
        S3_ENDPOINT_URL   full URL including bucket and path prefix
        S3_REGION_NAME    region of that endpoint
        the two from_env attributes should name whichever env vars hold the
        credentials for the new provider

    <storage_configuration>
        <disks>
            <cold_s3>
                <type>s3</type>
                <endpoint>S3_ENDPOINT_URL/cold_data/</endpoint>
                <region>S3_REGION_NAME</region>
                <access_key_id from_env="S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID"/>
                <secret_access_key from_env="S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"/>
                <connect_timeout_ms>5000</connect_timeout_ms>
                <request_timeout_ms>30000</request_timeout_ms>
                <retry_attempts>2</retry_attempts>
                <support_batch_delete>false</support_batch_delete>
                <metadata_path>/var/lib/clickhouse/disks/cold_s3/</metadata_path>
            </cold_s3>
            <s3_backup>
                <type>s3</type>
                <endpoint>S3_ENDPOINT_URL/backup/</endpoint>
                <region>S3_REGION_NAME</region>
                <access_key_id from_env="S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID"/>
                <secret_access_key from_env="S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"/>
                <connect_timeout_ms>5000</connect_timeout_ms>
                <request_timeout_ms>30000</request_timeout_ms>
                <retry_attempts>2</retry_attempts>
                <support_batch_delete>false</support_batch_delete>
                <metadata_path>/var/lib/clickhouse/disks/s3_backup/</metadata_path>
            </s3_backup>
        </disks>

        <policies>
            <hot_cold>
                <volumes>
                    <default>
                        <disk>default</disk>
                        <max_data_part_size_bytes>107374182400</max_data_part_size_bytes>
                    </default>
                    <cold>
                        <disk>cold_s3</disk>
                    </cold>
                </volumes>
            </hot_cold>

            <s3_policy>
                <volumes>
                    <main>
                        <disk>s3_backup</disk>
                    </main>
                </volumes>
            </s3_policy>
        </policies>

        <backups>
            <allowed_disk>s3_backup</allowed_disk>
            <allowed_path>.</allowed_path>
            <remove_backup_files_after_failure>true</remove_backup_files_after_failure>
        </backups>
    </storage_configuration>

      WARNING: re enabling hot_cold on its own does not move anything. The
      previous setup also relied on move_factor, which has already been removed;
      without it nothing spills to cold automatically. Re add it deliberately if
      that behaviour is wanted.
    -->

</clickhouse>
